    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fictīcĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		fictus, from fingo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>artificial</i>, <i>counterfeit</i>, <i>not genuine</i>, <i>fictitious</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 13, 76, § 199
				sq.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 16, 18, § 98</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					15, 7, 7, § 24</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Feigned</i>, <i>pretended</i>:
			actiones, Ulp. Regul. tit. 28, 12. —<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fictīcĭe</span></b> , <i>in
				pretence</i>: justi (Hilar.), Anon. ap. Job, 1, 15.</div>
